course: dictionary
lesson: 8248
title: Germs That Cause Colds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A rhinovirus is a very small germ, called a virus, that causes most colds. You cannot see it without a powerful microscope. «Colds are caused by viruses, most often rhinoviruses.»
explain: The word starts with «rhino», which is Greek for nose. That is a clue to where the germ works: it infects the nose and makes it runny and blocked.
explain: Rhinoviruses spread through coughs, sneezes and touching hands. Washing your hands and sneezing into a tissue help to stop them spreading. «Antibiotics do nothing against viruses.»
fact: A rhinovirus is a very small germ that is the most common cause of the common cold.
fact: Rhinoviruses are a kind of virus, and there are many different types of them.
fact: «Rhino» is Greek for nose, so the word tells you where the germ works.
fact: Rhinoviruses spread through coughs, sneezes and touching hands.
fact: Antibiotics do not work on viruses, so they cannot cure a cold.
exercise: «Colds are caused by viruses, most often rhinoviruses.» What is a rhinovirus? | A tissue used for sneezing | A large animal with a horn on its nose | A medicine that kills germs | *A very small germ that causes most colds
exercise: The word rhinovirus starts with «rhino», which is Greek for nose. Which part of the body does a rhinovirus infect? | The ears | The stomach | *The nose | The knee
exercise: Which of these helps stop rhinoviruses spreading? | *Washing your hands | Touching everything in the classroom | Sharing your cup with everyone | Sneezing into the air
test: Do antibiotics work against rhinoviruses? | Only on Sundays | *No, antibiotics do not work on viruses | Yes, always
test: «Going out with wet hair does not give you a cold.» Why not? | Cold air always makes you ill | Wet hair kills all germs | Wet hair is a kind of rhinovirus | *A cold is caused by a virus, not by wet hair
exam: What does «rhinovirus infection» mean? | An illness caused by a rhino at the zoo | A cold caused by wet hair | A cut on the hand that never heals | *An illness caused by a rhinovirus, usually in the nose
